# Browser (src/lib/browser.ts). Chromium's process sandbox is ON by default. On a host that restricts
# unprivileged user namespaces (Ubuntu 24.04), name a root-owned setuid sandbox helper; the production
# process manager config (ecosystem.config.cjs) sets it. Only BROWSER_SANDBOX=off turns the sandbox off
# (the Dockerfile does, for a root-in-container run); never set it in production.
# CHROME_DEVEL_SANDBOX=/opt/google/chrome/chrome-sandbox
# BROWSER_SANDBOX=
